problem_statement:
Expose warm_start in Isolation forest

It seems to me that sklearn.ensemble.IsolationForest supports incremental addition of new trees via the warm_start parameter inherited from its parent class, sklearn.ensemble.BaseBagging.

Even though this parameter is not exposed in the __init__() signature, it gets inherited from BaseBagging and one can use it by setting warm_start to True after initialization. To make it work, you also have to increment n_estimators on every iteration.

It took me a while to notice that it actually works, and I had to inspect the source code of both IsolationForest and BaseBagging. Also, it looks to me that the behavior is in-line with sklearn.ensemble.BaseForest that is behind e.g. sklearn.ensemble.RandomForestClassifier.

To make it easier to use, I'd suggest to:
* expose warm_start in IsolationForest.__init__(), default False;
* document it in the same way as it is documented for RandomForestClassifier — i.e. explain that warm_start is an optional boolean parameter (default False) and that when set to True the estimator should reuse the solution from the previous call to fit and add more estimators to the ensemble, otherwise a whole new forest is fitted; refer to the glossary entry for warm_start;
* add a test to make sure it works properly;
* possibly also mention it in the IsolationForest example documentation entry;

